name>Pellarin</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name><name><surname>Bangerter</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkins</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Pharmacologic consequences of cholesterol absorption inhibition: alteration in cholesterol metabolism and reduction in plasma cholesterol concentration induced by the synthetic saponin &#x003b2;-tigogenin cellobioside (CP-88818; tiqueside)</article-title><source>J Lipid Res</source><year>1993</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8468523</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vinson</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hu</surname><given-names>S-J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jung</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanski</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A citrus extract plus ascorbic acid decreases lipids, lipid peroxidation, lipoprotein oxidation susceptibility, and atherosclerosis in hypercholesterolemic hamsters</article-title><source>J Agric Food Chem</source><year>1998</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>1453</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kapoor</surname><given-names>LD</given-names></name></person-group><source>Handbook of Ayurvedic Medicinal Plants.</source><year>2001</year><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Herbal Reference Library Edition, CRC Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goyal</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surn